  "description": "Colonisation arrives in the form of religion. A Senegalese village kidnaps its own princess rather than surrender her to forced conversion, and the film stages the debate — Islam, Christianity, tradition — as open political theatre. Banned in Senegal for its spelling, of all things.\n\nThe Ceddo people try to preserve their traditional African culture against the onslaught of Islam, Christianity, and the slave trade. When King Demba War sides with the Muslims, the Ceddo kidnap his daughter, Princess Dior Yacine, to protest their forcible conversion to Islam.",
